5,1,1,talk,Minato,,I think we should look into the staffing of the coordination group and in-house developer availability to see if we have enough people to help.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Minato's focus on resources. I'll look into network coverage at customer plants and vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work to understand the external constraints.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,"I will examine the capital budget and software allowance, as well as the handling of vendor queries, to get a sense of our financial flexibility.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,I'll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. We need to know what actually sticks.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,I'll look into the time lost to copying existing records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs to see where the daily struggles are.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,"Does anyone else think we should check the vendor queries? @George, you mentioned it, but I wonder if that relates to the staffing issues I'm worried about.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It might. If the query volume is high, it could be straining the very staff Minato is concerned about. I'm curious if those bottlenecks are internal or caused by the vendors themselves.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"That is a fair point, Jonathan. I will keep that in mind while I review the handling of vendor queries to see if the issue is the process or the people.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"I'm more interested in the patterns of failure. If the standardization efforts failed, it doesn't matter how many people we have; we'll just be failing more efficiently.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,"I understand, May. I just hope that by looking at the incident logs and the time lost, we can find a project that solves a real, tangible problem for the staff.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,I think Midori is right. I hope the things we are looking into will show us how to make the work easier for everyone.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe that is the most sustainable approach. If we ignore the technical and environmental constraints, we risk funding a project that looks good on paper but fails in practice.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,I agree. It is better to be cautious now than to face an unexpected bill or a failed implementation later. I will focus on the budget details to ensure we are grounded in reality.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,I'll be the one to tell us if we're just repeating old mistakes. Let's see if the data supports the ambition of these proposals.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,I'm glad we're all on the same page. I'll focus on the ground-level data and report back on what the actual daily losses look like.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,I think we have a good plan. I'll stick with my choices and look forward to hearing what everyone else finds out.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
