40,2,1,talk,Minato,,"It seems we are short-staffed; the coordination group hasn't refilled any posts, and our developers are busy with the accounting upgrade until the third quarter.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is concerning. I found that network coverage at customer plants is very unreliable, with half the sites losing signal for whole afternoons, and getting device approval is a slow process.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital line is frozen, though we have some room in the software allowance. Also, it seems we are repeatedly asking vendors for the same certificates across different units.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,May,,"My findings are discouraging. The last three rollouts that required daily input from everyone were dropped, and most cross-unit standardization efforts ended without an owner. Only the narrow, trade-specific tools survived.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that we're losing nearly an hour every day to copying records that already exist, and there have been eleven misrouted deliveries this year because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, if the capital budget is frozen, does that mean we can only afford things that fit into the software allowance? I'm worried about who will do the work.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that's a key point. Given the developer shortage you mentioned, we should avoid anything requiring heavy custom build-out unless it's a fixed-fee project that doesn't rely on our internal team.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,George,,"Exactly. We must rely on the software allowance, and as Jonathan suggests, we should be wary of any project that demands significant internal developer time or new capital expenditure.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,May,,"And based on my research, we should also avoid anything that requires daily input from everyone. If it's a broad, company-wide tool, it'll likely be dropped just like the last three.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Midori,,"That makes me think we should prioritize something that solves the record-copying and delivery issues, as those are clear, daily losses that don't necessarily require everyone's constant input.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I agree with Midori. If we can fix the record-copying and delivery problems without overloading the few people we have left, it would be a huge help.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"But we must be careful. If the solution requires a mobile app for field use, my findings on network coverage and device approval suggest it might be a technical nightmare to implement.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,George,,I agree with Jonathan. We cannot ignore the network issues. We need a solution that is financially sustainable and technically feasible given our current constraints.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,May,,"So we need something narrow in scope, low on internal developer demand, and not dependent on a perfect network. It sounds like we're looking for a very specific kind of tool.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Midori,,Maybe a central repository for data would work? It could stop the record-copying and the delivery errors without needing a mobile app or constant input from every single employee.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Minato,,That sounds like a very safe and helpful choice. It would address the problems Midori found without needing the developers I'm worried about.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. A centralized data approach avoids the network pitfalls of a field app and, if handled via a vendor with fixed-fee work, wouldn't strain our internal developers.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,George,,"It would also fit within our software allowance and solve the redundant vendor queries I discovered, making it a fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,May,,"It also avoids the trap of requiring daily input from everyone, as it's more of a reference tool than a task-management one. It seems we've found a common ground.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm glad we've found a direction that balances the practical needs of the staff with our current limitations. I look forward to seeing the candidates.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
